      "writtenOn": "2025-07-04T08:07:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I agree. I\u0027ll try to suppress the message, at least when comparing against the specified parents. I\u0027ll first need to reproduce it locally.\n\nThanks! Sounds good!\n\n\u003e As for the branch - I do need it in 3.10, but I\u0027m fine maintaining it as a patch for the time being.\n\nPersonally I don\u0027t mind much, as at Google we are anyway always using the latest master. So I guess it depends on what the release maintainers think about this.\n\n\u003e That said, I think a \"bad UI experience\" is still much better than an\n\u003e \"internal server error\" on push.\n\nIf it\u0027s an internal server error at the moment, then we could fix this and reject the push with a proper error message saying that criss-cross merges are not supported. I agree that we should not fail with an internal server error and that\u0027s a bad user experience too.",
